          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Take steaks out of the fridge 1 hour before cooking."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat a griddle pan until smoking hot. Pat steaks dry."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season steaks generously on both sides with salt and pepper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Lay steaks on the griddle. Cook for 4 to 5 minutes without moving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Flip once. Cook another 4 to 5 minutes for medium-rare."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stand the steaks upright on the bone edge for 2 minutes if using T-bone."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove to a board. Rest for 10 minutes. Do not cover."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drizzle with olive oil. Add rosemary sprigs. Serve with lemon wedges and white beans or salad."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "No crust formed",
              "cause": "Pan not hot enough or steak was wet",
              "fix": "Get the pan smoking before adding the steak. Pat steaks dry first."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Steak is chewy",
              "cause": "Sliced too soon or cut with the grain",
              "fix": "Rest fully for 10 minutes. Slice against the grain."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Overcooked in the middle",
              "cause": "Steak was cold from the fridge",
              "fix": "Always bring steaks to room temperature before cooking."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bistecca alla fiorentina is considered sacred in Tuscany. The Chianina breed of cattle, native to the Tuscan and Umbrian valleys, produces the pale, lean beef traditionally used. The T-bone cut is sold by weight at the table in Florentine restaurants. Tuscans are proud that the dish needs almost nothing: good beef, salt, heat, and time. The name bistecca comes from the English word beefsteak, acquired by Florentines watching English traders grill meat in the 18th century."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
